    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "Hey!\r\n\r\nThis is actually expected. Triton is not tuned for Turing. On the RTX2080 it's using the Volta `mma.884` instructions which operates at half the throughput of `mma.1688`. This is why you see it showing roughly half the performance of cuBLAS in your benchmark. @daadaada any interest in improving support for Turing? If RTX2080 supports mma.16816, we could just re-use the same code-path as A100 when lowering the `dot` instruction.",
